### Turn 3 — follow-up on the same result (no new tool call)

**User:** `Who represented the plaintiff in that case?`

Per §5.3, this is a follow-up referencing "that case" -- the previous tool result is still in
`conversation.last_results` and in the Gemini conversation history, so the system prompt instructs
the model not to call the tool again ("Do NOT call search_judgments again unless a new search is
needed"). Gemini answers from the prior turn's retrieved snippet instead.

```json
{
  "query": "Who represented the plaintiff in that case?",
  "answer": "Based on the previous result, I don't have the advocate's name in the retrieved snippet -- would you like me to run a fresh search specifically for that detail?",
  "tool_used": null,
  "results": []
}
```

*(This turn also shows an honest limitation: the tool's `snippet` field truncates chunk text to
500 characters, so follow-up questions about details outside that window sometimes can't be
answered from history alone -- Gemini should ideally offer a fresh search rather than guessing,
which is what the system prompt's "if information is unavailable, clearly say so" rule is for.)*

